<title>USA: U.S. farmers plant most corn, soybean since 1980s.</title>
<headline>U.S. farmers plant most corn, soybean since 1980s.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-06-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Good weather combined with favorable prices have spurred U.S. farmers to plant their largest corn and soybean crops since the 1980s, the U.S. Agriculture Department said on Monday.</p>
<p>In its annual Acreage Report, the department estimated this year's corn plantings at 80.2 million acres, up 1 percent from last year and the highest since 1985.</p>
<p>The rise in soybean plantings was even more impressive.</p>
<p>Based on its survey of farmers during the first 2 weeks of June, the department estimated soybean plantings at 70.9 million, up 10 percent from 1996 and the largest since 1982.</p>
</text>
